From 83afb3c5eed0c0a5d2bde2a0e4063a7a8751ac98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael P Jones <QuixoticSeven@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:54:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fm1-soc: model the P33 power-domain bridge and its register
 file

JL_P33 (0x13E00: PMU_CON, RTC_CON, SPI_CON, SPI_DAT) was unknown MMIO, so
every P33 read returned 0. Firmwares that read back what they wrote saw
their writes vanish: Melodee 1.4 verifies its stock-V15 supply setup
(P3_ANA_CON0/5/6/9) and, when the check fails, never starts CPU1 or (in
its no-fallback build) halts before the LCD is initialised.

The bridge now shifts three-byte frames (op/address-high, address-low,
data) into a 2 x 1 KiB register file (P33 bank, RTC bank via SPI_CON bit
8); write/or/and/xor update a register, a read returns it in SPI_DAT.
Transfers finish at once (busy bit 1 reads 0, as before). Registers reset
to 0, so a firmware that only writes P33 sees no change. FM1_P33_TRACE
prints each frame.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 crates/fm1-soc/src/lib.rs |   9 ++
 crates/fm1-soc/src/p33.rs | 171 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 docs/stock-firmware.md    |   1 +
